{\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\",\"id\":\"continuation-write-report-1\",\"operation\":\"work.write\",\"arguments\":{\"grant_id\":\"urn:stdo-skills:qualification:codex:recovery-histories:write\",\"target\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"outputs/continuation.md\",\"object\":null,\"sha256\":\"acd5d1278fbabc1387c741dd135a007bafc417631d9be4cbbefca4aeb7e22d65\",\"selector\":null},\"mode\":\"replace\",\"record\":{\"text\":\"# Continuation report\\n\\nThis report applies R1 in [specification/REQUIREMENT.md](../specification/REQUIREMENT.md) and D1 in [design/DESIGN.md](../design/DESIGN.md), under the bounded authority in [TASK.md](../TASK.md). It resumes the continuation decisions for the six jobs; the authorized effect is this report alone.\\n\\n[HISTORY-BOUNDARY.md](../HISTORY-BOUNDARY.md) stipulates that the histories are controlled scenario inputs supplied by the fixture preparer. They are not authenticated reviews, actual historical production executions, or Root acceptance. Every retained assessment, owner disposition, and work state below has that conditional standing. Each job is an independent snapshot: an event in B is not a new observation in A, even where candidate bytes and assessment identifiers coincide.\\n\\nThe current host actually acquired the files, checked their SHA-256 identities, compared the supplied text, and checked candidate presence. Those observations establish the cited byte facts; they do not authenticate the simulated history or execute the selected renderer. No simulated job was constructed, repaired, reviewed, accepted, previewed, or published during this report task.\\n\\n## A-current\\n\\nEvidence: [jobs/A-current/history.json](../jobs/A-current/history.json) — SHA-256 "'`a6be8d433580052df3c43155022c2a9c09d41de8997e953b7238d4b950715085`. Deciding fields: `/assessment`, `/domain`, `/owner_disposition`, `/selected_next`, and `/unresolved_counterexamples`.'"\\n\\nPhysical candidate: [jobs/A-current/candidate.json](../jobs/A-current/candidate.json) — SHA-256 "'`8b6bd00da7be7b289ca0d28e1d3d4fec77c1172ced31194812eb8c73f09a09e8`. Governing input: [jobs/A-current/requirement.txt](../jobs/A-current/requirement.txt) — SHA-256 `42d474e2d82c9bac0a42324377aa63c944fb0c3cb6d2f5fe33bbd77d7a95da8c`. Both current hashes match the history'"'s exact subject and requirement.\\n\\n**Retained result and current reliance.** "'`sample-assessment-1` records `satisfied` for “selected renderer returns the required greeting for both domain names,” with domain `Ada`, `Zoë` and evidence `Hello, Ada.'"\\\\n"'`, `Hello, Zoë.'"\\\\n"'`. Here `'"\\\\n"'` denotes one newline. The history records acceptance for the next selected local preview preparation, with controlled-history standing only. Its currentness condition is “applicable until conflicting observation or basis change.” Neither invalidator occurs in A'"'s supplied snapshot, so the predicate remains established conditionally on that snapshot and exact domain. The candidate's availability, retained assessment, and limited disposition are separate facts.\\n\\n**Supported continuation and remaining work.** Retain that assessment and report eligibility for the selected local preview preparation. The preview effect must be separately admitted, as "'`/selected_next` explicitly requires; this report grant does not admit it. No preview execution, broader-domain fitness, production acceptance, or publication is supplied. No fresh assessment is required merely because this is a resumption. A later applicable counterexample or material change to the candidate, renderer, requirement, or assessment basis would require reconsidering the affected reliance.'"\\n\\n## B-counterexample\\n\\nEvidence: [jobs/B-counterexample/history.json](../jobs/B-counterexample/history.json) — SHA-256 "'`4a59092211bb916ff21709505ee0d4bfced6ac0d316709d12187d3397e9df1a4`. Deciding fields: `/assessment`, `/owner_disposition`, and `/unresolved_counterexamples/0`.'"\\n\\nPhysical candidate: [jobs/B-counterexample/candidate.json](../jobs/B-counterexample/candidate.json) — SHA-256 "'`8b6bd00da7be7b289ca0d28e1d3d4fec77c1172ced31194812eb8c73f09a09e8`. Governing input: [jobs/B-counterexample/requirement.txt](../jobs/B-counterexample/requirement.txt) — SHA-256 `42d474e2d82c9bac0a42324377aa63c944fb0c3cb6d2f5fe33bbd77d7a95da8c`. Both current hashes match B'"'s recorded identities and the counterexample's identities. The candidate bytes also equal A's bytes.\\n\\n**Retained result and current reliance.** B retains the earlier "'`sample-assessment-1` satisfaction and limited owner disposition, but also retains the later, unresolved `ce-render-zoe`. On input `Zoë`, it records actual output `Hello, .'"\\\\n"'` against required output `Hello, Zoë.'"\\\\n"'`, after the earlier assessment, on the same candidate and requirement. This is an applicable counterexample to the predicate covering both domain names. On the stipulated evidence that predicate is falsified, and the earlier satisfied result cannot support preview eligibility. Equal candidate hashes do not erase the later evidence. Preserve the earlier assessment, disposition, and Ada observation as historical evidence; none disposes the Zoë defect.'"\\n\\n**Supported continuation and remaining work.** Withhold reliance on the prior acceptance for preview preparation. Carry "'`ce-render-zoe` to the implementation/renderer repair owner under a separate grant, then obtain assessment of the exact repaired subject and current requirement over the retained domain, explicitly resolving the counterexample. The present record supplies no repair, superseding assessment, renewed disposition, or preview effect. The template file alone does not identify the renderer'"'s implementation defect, so this report does not invent a fix.\\n\\n## C-stale\\n\\nEvidence: [jobs/C-stale/history.json](../jobs/C-stale/history.json) — SHA-256 "'`5f8bfad24353770c8baef6a0d4009b7622e6d8998b8816f04b637b98fedaa084`. Deciding fields: `/old_assessment`, `/current_governing_source`, `/current_governing_sha256`, `/unaffected_observation`, and `/reassessment`.'"\\n\\nPhysical candidate: [jobs/C-stale/candidate.txt](../jobs/C-stale/candidate.txt) — SHA-256 "'`8b1560f395c0248eca4d2d6cc361825a9f8c00d11ce6f52b26eea2872573c2c1`. Old basis: [jobs/C-stale/requirement-old.txt](../jobs/C-stale/requirement-old.txt) — SHA-256 `3599b98fcf45dba3761294d21eb721d03551060162793ebeb3b88ca9e173a9c3`. Current basis: [jobs/C-stale/requirement-current.txt](../jobs/C-stale/requirement-current.txt) — SHA-256 `fc6bf475a002a86aeacaa5981e52b91962928084a06e08ae0e4f194c7f0414c8`. Each acquired hash matches its respective recorded identity; the old and current requirements are different.'"\\n\\n**Retained result and current reliance.** "'`punctuation-review-old` records `satisfied` against the old requirement, which asks for `Hello, Ada.'"\\\\n"'`. The candidate still contains those exact bytes. The current requirement instead asks for `Hello, Ada!'"\\\\n"'`. The changed governing basis invalidates direct reliance on the old satisfaction for the current requirement; it does not erase the old result on its old basis. The current text comparison also identifies the concrete punctuation mismatch. That comparison is a fresh report observation, not a fabricated historical review: `/reassessment` remains `not performed`, and no current satisfied assessment is supplied.'"\\n\\n**Unaffected evidence.** [unrelated/sentinel.txt](../unrelated/sentinel.txt) — SHA-256 "'`56686d9c77cc9592aee6e2e4514fe02a7f59daa3c0befced80b3980bc6cb51b3`. Its current bytes match `/unaffected_observation/sha256`, so the recorded sentinel-identity predicate remains established. The punctuation requirement change does not invalidate this independent byte-identity observation.'"\\n\\n**Supported continuation and remaining work.** Use the acquired current requirement as the repair and assessment basis. Route the punctuation repair to the implementation owner under a separate grant, then assess the exact resulting candidate against that requirement. Preserve the old assessment, old source, and unaffected sentinel evidence. No repair, current reassessment, or acceptance is recorded by this task.\\n\\n## D-construction-exhausted\\n\\nEvidence: [jobs/D-construction-exhausted/history.json](../jobs/D-construction-exhausted/history.json) — SHA-256 "'`cba1352b70fc4da4f9e0f28f59110cd2d9db5d3b65cf0f034affb53c9d6da4d9`. Deciding fields: `/operation`, `/performed`, `/bound`, `/stop`, `/required_output`, `/candidate_available`, `/assessment_performed`, and `/residual`.'"\\n\\n**Retained result and current reliance.** The construction operation was performed under a "'`2 steps` bound and stopped because the bound was exhausted before candidate publication. The required `jobs/D-construction-exhausted/candidate.json` is absent in the current snapshot, consistent with `candidate_available: false`. The supported construction status is `incomplete`; its core mapping is `falsified` for the predicate “a candidate is available.” This is an availability result, not a fitness judgment. `assessment_performed: false` means no candidate fitness result exists; it must not be labelled `indeterminate` or `falsified` for fitness.'"\\n\\n**Supported continuation and remaining work.** Preserve the stop cause and residual. Select and admit a sufficient construction bound, finish the required candidate and retain its transition evidence, then perform the required fitness assessment on that exact subject. The current report creates neither a candidate nor an assessment. Resource exhaustion alone supplies neither an owner-valid refusal nor a basis-change result.\\n\\n## E-performed-indeterminate\\n\\nEvidence: [jobs/E-performed-indeterminate/history.json](../jobs/E-performed-indeterminate/history.json) — SHA-256 "'`7fc9e148eec458bce92e9070ded4e9b84c4a9b533147dfd447e68bf6badf3296`; [jobs/E-performed-indeterminate/evidence.txt](../jobs/E-performed-indeterminate/evidence.txt) — SHA-256 `657938c4faf1a0e8cbd54a1cf569436d40b0a8c9426ad7d0824d65bc8cb42c39`. Deciding history fields: `/performed`, `/predicate`, `/result`, `/reason`, `/evidence`, and `/candidate_available`.'"\\n\\n**Retained result and current reliance.** The temperature assessment was performed and returned "'`indeterminate` for “temperature exceeded 20 degrees at the selected instant.” The admitted evidence records sensor A at 18 degrees and sensor B at 23 degrees, with no admitted precedence or error bound. Preserve both observations and the performed assessment. The predicate is neither established nor falsified by a deciding relation in the supplied evidence; the `indeterminate` result remains the supported result. `candidate_available: true` is retained as a scenario premise, separate from fitness. No physical candidate path or digest is supplied for that availability claim, so none is invented.'"\\n\\n**Supported continuation and remaining work.** Obtain admissible evidence or an authorized deciding relation sufficient for the selected instant, such as justified sensor precedence or error bounds, and reassess on that explicit basis. No such addition is currently supplied. Arbitrarily choosing a sensor or averaging their readings would introduce an unsupported rule. Keep the uncertainty open until the evidence can decide it; this is a performed undecidable assessment, not unperformed work.\\n\\n## F-unperformed\\n\\nEvidence: [jobs/F-unperformed/history.json](../jobs/F-unperformed/history.json) — SHA-256 "'`dd50153f2e605b7edad1b698342247debaf26318c7ef8a404a000df1c35f0625`. Deciding fields: `/candidate_available`, `/candidate`, `/planned_predicate`, `/assessment_performed`, `/assessment_result`, `/stop`, and `/residual`.'"\\n\\n**Retained result and current reliance.** The history stipulates an available “retained candidate under its own exact subject,” but supplies no physical candidate path or digest. Preserve that availability premise without manufacturing an identity or constructing a replacement. The planned fitness assessment was never activated before the resource stop: "'`assessment_performed: false`, `assessment_result: null`. Its status is `not_performed`, meaning no assessment result, rather than an `indeterminate` assessment. The planned fitness predicate is unestablished because it was not evaluated.'"\\n\\n**Supported continuation and remaining work.** Acquire and bind the retained candidate's exact subject and selected fitness requirement, then activate and perform the required assessment with sufficient authorized resources. Carry "'`perform required assessment` as the open obligation. No prior fitness judgment, acceptance, or publication can be consumed. E'"'s performed uncertainty and D's missing construction output do not supply a result for F.\\n\\n## Report basis and return boundary\\n\\nThe selected Product is "'`urn:stdo:product-definition:qualification-continuation`: [fixture_product.json](../fixture_product.json) — SHA-256 `983558d3a08de4f4fed107505e069e6ccae8bd3d7b75d3e3d8daba0dae9164d5`. Governing report sources: [specification/REQUIREMENT.md](../specification/REQUIREMENT.md) — SHA-256 `badc8c2607104f8df45c7297655ab719a2b62201752a1bd8082b1461b8348331`; [design/DESIGN.md](../design/DESIGN.md) — SHA-256 `2132ac2a6dc18133b22ff72b3ffd1563522b9f0ab4fef521b6d4d601fe909e8b`; [TASK.md](../TASK.md) — SHA-256 `22498f8609a7139c422ca9d6f1ea1517ba6eb867517404e43aaac682cc1945cf`. Provenance boundary: [HISTORY-BOUNDARY.md](../HISTORY-BOUNDARY.md) — SHA-256 `e42a0b93f9c37aeb1b463a4e23c9d11a4b43df691e4b3d6f7208cb8c5b96e069`.'"\\n\\n"'`stdo status --verify` reported the selected installation installed and valid, with no failures: `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest SHA-256 `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`. The deciding method source was `standards/ACTIVATION.md`, SHA-256 `56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d`: results and construction availability (§3), restart (§5), and exact applicability/invalidation (§7). Native `source.read` acquired the cited report inputs and retained job files by exact digest.'"\\n\\nThe actual author is this Codex host, principal "'`host`, actor `urn:stdo-skills:qualification:codex:recovery-histories:host`, under the bounded report task and grant `urn:stdo-skills:qualification:codex:recovery-histories:write`. The designated evidence consumer is `qualification-executive`; the report is returned to the requesting user. This is author analysis, with no independent reviewer or owner acceptance asserted. The observed CLI version is `codex-cli 0.164.0`; resolved model/effort and resource usage were not independently established.'"\\n\\nNative MCP discovery calls were blocked by the session's approval policy before operation execution. The exact CLI declared in "'`TOOLING.md` successfully supplied native discovery and source acquisition under policy SHA-256 `df795635470aa29b2a6542fc8d598a8797ee9138b24f73764c0c5f1f06f9ca38`, method profile `urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, profile SHA-256 `a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`. The transport limitation changes no job'"'s simulated result. A read-only Git status probe found that this workspace is not a Git repository; scope preservation is checked with file identities.\\n\\nThe output preimage was "'`# Pending continuation report'"\\\\n"'`, SHA-256 `acd5d1278fbabc1387c741dd135a007bafc417631d9be4cbbefca4aeb7e22d65`, acquired separately from governing inputs. The report'"'s native write response and subsequent postimage verification belong to the actual host-run evidence, not to any job history. No native conjunction is selected or claimed. Material changes to a cited subject, requirement, observation, authority, or provenance boundary require rechecking only affected reliance; all remaining job obligations stated above stay open.\\n\",\"provenance\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\".qualification/OWNER.json\",\"object\":null,\"sha256\":\"fa7498cff3f73cab274d7b0ea4f1256c6a0c364636b187cb94bd4512643c387b\",\"selector\":null}},\"interpretation\":null,\"observations\":[{\"id\":\"sha256:025905ada3e3ed2df11f15d377c809aeb5595588966d4793be349adf1703b2b8\",\"sha256\":\"025905ada3e3ed2df11f15d377c809aeb5595588966d4793be349adf1703b2b8\"}]}}
